  "ch3.title": "Northbridge and southbridge",
  "ch3.law": "In the northbridge era, data from the CPU, graphics card, disk and network card all ended up at one memory controller in the northbridge. The wires had become point-to-point, but the meeting point was still shared.",
  "ch3.p1": "Once the shared bus could no longer keep up, motherboards made a compromise: take the fastest devices off the shared bus and give each its own wire to one chip. That chip, drawn at the top of motherboard diagrams, is the <strong>northbridge</strong> (Intel called it the MCH, memory controller hub). Slower interfaces went to a second chip, drawn lower down: the <strong>southbridge</strong> (ICH, I/O controller hub).",
  "ch3.p2": "Take Intel’s 875P, from its 2004 datasheet, as an example. The CPU connects to the northbridge over a 64-bit <strong>front-side bus</strong>, peaking at {fsbG} GB/s. The northbridge drives two DDR400 memory channels, {memG} GB/s together. The graphics card uses a dedicated AGP 8X slot at {agpG} GB/s, and a gigabit network port uses a dedicated CSA link at {csaM} MB/s. The southbridge hangs below the northbridge on a <strong>{hiM} MB/s</strong> Hub Interface. It handles two SATA ports, IDE, {usbPorts} USB 2.0 ports, PCI slots and the flash chip that stores the BIOS.",
  "ch3.p3": "The most important part of this diagram is the northbridge: anyone who reads or writes memory has to go through its memory controller. The model below hands each traffic source’s demand to these links, and shares bandwidth by <strong>max-min fairness</strong>. Each link splits its capacity as evenly as it can among the flows crossing it, and whatever a flow does not need is passed on to the others.",
  "ch3.model.title": "How memory bandwidth is shared on a 2004 PC",
  "ch3.model.how": "Drag the memory bandwidth that the CPU, the graphics card and the southbridge devices each want, and tick the network card if it is receiving. Each row shows how busy one link is: grey is what is wanted, colour is what is actually delivered.",
  "ch3.model.aria": "Load on each link of the 875P platform: front-side bus, memory, AGP, Hub Interface and CSA",
  "ch3.ctl.cpu": "CPU wants",
  "ch3.ctl.gpu": "Graphics card wants",
